> Telemetry's and RUM's dashboards are both served on telemetry.betterstack.com and rum.betterstack.com. <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`product`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Product`" pulumi-lang-go="`product`" pulumi-lang-python="`product`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`product`" pulumi-lang-java="`product`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`product`">`product`</span> says which one a dashboard belongs to.

> Dashboard templates are a separate resource. List them via [List dashboard templates](https://betterstack.com/docs/logs/api/dashboards/templates/).

## Import

Import an existing dashboard by its ID. Get the ID from the matching get function, which finds it by <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`dashboardGroupId`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`DashboardGroupId`" pulumi-lang-go="`dashboardGroupId`" pulumi-lang-python="`dashboard_group_id`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`dashboardGroupId`" pulumi-lang-java="`dashboardGroupId`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`dashboard_group_id`">`dashboardGroupId`</span> or <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`name`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Name`" pulumi-lang-go="`name`" pulumi-lang-python="`name`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`name`" pulumi-lang-java="`name`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`name`">`name`</span>.

```sh
$ pulumi import betterstack:index/dashboard:Dashboard example 12345
```

